WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.193
Which cloud you're in decides which Graph

2
00:00:02.193 --> 00:00:04.525
host you call and where
your token comes from.

3
00:00:04.525 --> 00:00:08.537
A G C C tenant like this estate's
uses the worldwide endpoints,

4
00:00:08.537 --> 00:00:13.912
so Microsoft's sample works here as written,
even though its address is hard-coded.

5
00:00:13.912 --> 00:00:17.879
Sending a batch and reading
the results are both available,

6
00:00:17.879 --> 00:00:20.550
because GCC uses the worldwide service.

7
00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:23.749
The hardened client takes
its endpoint from settings

8
00:00:23.749 --> 00:00:26.450
and only accepts a host
on its Graph allow-list.

9
00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:29.090
Now let's see what Microsoft
actually gives you.
